If a patient has a depression then the patient has a higher-opioid-harm-risk.
If a patient has a mental-health-condition then the patient has a higher-opioid-harm-risk.
If a patient has a substance-use-disorder-history then the patient has a higher-opioid-harm-risk.
If a patient has an overdose-history then the patient has a higher-opioid-harm-risk.
If a patient has a combined-opioid-dosage and the combined-opioid-dosage includes at least 50 MME-units-per-day then the patient has a higher-opioid-harm-risk.
If a patient takes a central-nervous-system-depressant with an opioid then the patient has a higher-opioid-harm-risk.
If a patient has a higher-opioid-harm-risk then every clinician should reevaluate the patient at an interval of less than 3 months.
